{
  "version": "0.6.2",
  "notes": "0.6.1's HTTPREAD chunk fix still dropped exactly one whole chunk on the very next real run (AT+HTTPACTION declared 3393 bytes, only 2369 came back -- 1024 short, matching one full chunk -- with no error raised at all). Root cause not yet pinned down (a clean synthetic reproduction of the same chunk-size pattern reassembles correctly), so instead of guessing further: parse_http_read() now takes the already-known expected_length (from AT+HTTPACTION) and raises a clear CellularError if the reassembled size doesn't match, instead of silently returning truncated data that fails later with a cryptic JSON error. Also prints each chunk found (index/declared length/actual length) so the next real run's Thonny output shows exactly where a chunk goes missing, if it happens again.",
